# Subscription auth (recommended) — bills your Claude subscription, no per-token charges.
# Get one with: `claude setup-token`
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Pay-per-token API auth (alternative). Either is fine; CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN takes precedence inside Claude Code.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# GitHub auth on the HOST: baywatch shells out to `gh` on the host for issue/PR fetches and diffs.
# Just `gh auth login` once — no env var needed for host-side gh.

# GitHub auth INSIDE the sandbox: a fine-grained PAT with READ-ONLY scopes (Contents: read,
# Issues: read, PRs: read, Metadata: read). The agent's `gh` inside the container uses this.
# Read-only at the token level means even if the deny rules slipped, gh writes would 401 at GitHub.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
